%% Regalis WorkSpace — booking lifecycle
%% generated from enum BookingStatus (backend/src/Regalis.Domain/Enums/BookingEnums.cs)
%% Transitions verified against the assigning call sites, cited per edge.
%% Every transition below also writes a TRN_BookingStatusHistory row.

stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB

  [*] --> Pending : booking created

  Pending --> Confirmed : payment captured
  Pending --> Expired : Booking.PendingHoldMinutes elapsed
  Pending --> Cancelled : cancelled before start

  Confirmed --> CheckedIn : gate scan or self check-in
  Confirmed --> Cancelled : cancelled before start
  Confirmed --> Confirmed : rescheduled

  CheckedIn --> Completed : check-out

  Completed --> [*]
  Cancelled --> [*]
  Expired --> [*]

  note right of Pending
    Created by BookingService (:110 customer, :242 pass/admin).
    Holds the slot for Booking.PendingHoldMinutes (default 10).
    Expiry is swept by the BookingHoldSweeper background job.
  end note

  note right of Confirmed
    Reschedule keeps the status at Confirmed but still records a
    history row (BookingMutationService :159).
  end note

  note right of CheckedIn
    In  : AccessService :364 (gate) / AttendanceService :142 (app)
    Out : AccessService :370 (gate) / AttendanceService :161 (app)
  end note

  note right of Cancelled
    Guard: status must be Pending or Confirmed AND StartUtc > now.
    A Confirmed + Paid booking refunds, setting PaymentStatus to
    Refunded or PartiallyRefunded.
  end note

%% NoShow (BookingStatus = 7) is intentionally absent as a transition.
%% It is declared in the enum and read once as a terminal-state filter
%% (BookingService :538), but no code path ever assigns it. Add the edge
%% Confirmed --> NoShow only once a sweeper or admin action sets it.
%%
%% BookingPaymentStatus (Pending/Paid/Failed/Refunded/PartiallyRefunded)
%% is a separate axis and deliberately not merged into these states.
